UseRef:
We can use useRef for 2 scenarios.
1) For value Persistance                          2)To access or update the directly dom elements

 For value Persistance :
 
import { useState } from "react";

const Body = () => {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  let val=1;
  const incrementCount = () => {
    val=val+1
    console.log(val);      {/*val variable apni value ko persist/hold ni rkh pa rha kyu k ye har re-render pr 1 sy initialize hu jata ha,to prevent it,we can use useRef instead of local variable*/}
    
    setCount((count) => count + 1);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <h1>{count} Parent   {val}</h1>
      <br />
      <br />
      <button onClick={incrementCount}>Increment Count</button>
      <br />
      <br />
    </>
  );
};
export default Body;

Now ,how useRef persist the value even on re render because useRef returns an object.Its means below variable named val is an object.In this object,a  special field is avaiable by which you can set or get the data.That field is current.Its means ,currently 0 is avaiable in its current value.

let val=useRef(0); 

Now see below example:
